From f2640f6e839651a417032e31b181e11d91daa377 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sri <sri.bng@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 03:31:18 +1000
Subject: [PATCH] Move RingCentral sign-in server-side and add Service Quality
 from the Business Analytics API

The dashboard now runs on a Cloudflare Worker (worker/) that holds the JWT app
credentials in its secrets, signs in to RingCentral itself, and serves a
read-only JSON API under /api/. Viewers enter one shared dashboard password in
Settings instead of doing OAuth/PKCE or picking a credentials file in the
browser; those browser-side flows are removed.

The Service Quality tab is no longer upload-only: /api/qos pulls the
Business Analytics timeline grouped by call queue (service level from the
queue SLA counters, speed of answer and handle time from the answered-call
segment timers) and maps it to the existing QosRecord shape.

Also: Worker tests against a fake RingCentral (npm test), a Cloudflare deploy
workflow, wrangler config, and README setup steps.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
